  "documentation": {
    "content": "Check for the drive type. \n\ndisk show -fields type, model\n\nIf it is X670_TPM5V15TATE NA55, then contact support and get the drive replaced asap. \n\nThe working theory is that a \"corrosive agent\" (potentially a cleaner of some kind) needs to be introduced into the environment where these drives are physically present. This particular drive has an inlet for ambient air to help with cooling. This inlet can allow contaminants to interact with NAND chips on the drives internal systems which leads to corrosion. \n\n${metric_or_resource.labels}",
